{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Moses took the anointing oil, and anointed the Tabernacle, and poured of the anointing oil upon Aaron's head</b> — This too Moses did in proper order, for thus he was commanded in the matter of the making of the oil (Exodus 30:26–30): \"And you shall anoint with it the Tent, etc., and Aaron and his sons you shall anoint.\" Therefore he did not want to anoint the Tabernacle until he clothed Aaron and anointed them together, so that the one who offers would be ready to come into the sanctuary to perform the service. And for Aaron it was sufficient that he is holy to HaShem, even though in the commandment of erecting the Tabernacle it is written (Exodus 40:9), \"And you shall anoint the Tabernacle and all that is in it,\" and afterward, \"And you shall bring near Aaron and his sons, etc., and you shall wash them and clothe Aaron\" (ibid. verses 12–13), for there he arranged everything done for Aaron and his sons together."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:51:37.985275485Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}